#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "The EMIS domain model"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "This page describes the data an education management information system holds, how that data is divided into domains, and the rules every implementation follows when it models them. The capabilities describe the platform; this page describes the data the platform exists for."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Code lists and local terms vary from country to country, but the resources and rules below don't. Every term on this page is defined in the vocabulary of its bounded context, and you'll find the contexts listed in the [context map]{1}. How the contexts themselves are designed is covered in [domain design]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Domains"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Each domain is a catalog in each environment, named `<domain>_<env>` ([CAP-CATALOG.2]{1}), and each has one steward who owns it. A resource lives in exactly one domain. Other domains refer to it, but they never copy it. Each domain also belongs to one bounded context, although a context may own several domains ([domain design]{2})."
msgstr ""

