#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "The registries of [CAP-MASTERDATA]{1} are split by what they identify. Persons are in `people`, institutions and sites are in `institutions`, and posts are in `workforce`. There's no separate registry of learners, staff members or guardians, because those are roles a person holds through relationships ([ADR-0010]{2}). The `reference` domain holds the code lists and the data dictionary of [CAP-REFERENCE]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Core resources and relationships"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Every relationship and fact also belongs to an academic period and uses governed code lists. We've left those links out of the drawing to keep it readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Why it is drawn this way"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**One person, many roles.** A person is recorded once, whether they're a learner, a guardian or a staff member, and over a lifetime they may be all three. The roles are relationships, not separate registries ([ADR-0010]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Institutions occupy sites.** Two institutions can share one site on different shifts, and one institution can work from several sites. So the link between them is a relationship with dates. Facilities belong to the site, and you read an institution's services through its occupancy."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Enrolment and class membership are separate.** A learner is enrolled in one programme and grade, but they may be taught in a class that spans grades, or take one subject with a higher grade."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**A post is not a person.** Shortages and vacancies are the difference between the posts and the people posted to them. A posting records its share of full time, so a teacher who works at two institutions is counted correctly, whether you count heads or full-time equivalents."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Facts belong to relationships.** That way an attendance session or a result can always be traced to an enrolment in a specific period."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Modelling rules"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Identifiers mean nothing and never change.** An identifier carries no information about the person or thing it identifies, and a learner keeps the same one for life ([CAP-MASTERDATA]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Every relationship that changes is effective-dated.** It records when it was valid from, when it was valid to, and when it was recorded. A correction adds a new version, so history is never edited ([P18]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Store events and counts, and derive every rate.** Attendance rates, ratios and percentages are computed from counts in the semantic layer. They're never stored on records, because you can't re-aggregate a stored rate to a different level ([CAP-TRANSFORMATION.5]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**An attribute with several values becomes rows.** A list of languages or subjects is a child table that refers to a code list, not a delimited string or an embedded document. Bronze may hold the data as it was received, and silver normalises it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Every coded attribute names its code list and its version** ([CAP-REFERENCE.1]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Status and reason are kept apart.** An enrolment has a state (active, suspended or ended) and, once it ends, an exit reason (completed, transferred, left the education system or deceased). If you mix the two, you can no longer tell a transfer from a dropout."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Repetition and promotion are derived.** They follow from the progression decision and the next period's enrolment, never from a stored flag. So when either is corrected, the correction shows up everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Formats are fixed once,** in the data dictionary, and never system by system ([CAP-REFERENCE.6]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Documents are records.** A certificate, plan or medical note attached to a record is stored by its content hash, classified at least as high as the record, and kept for as long as the record's retention class says ([CAP-RECORDS]{1})."
msgstr ""

